# Docker / nginx

## Services

`db` (pgvector), `api`, `worker` (B7: outbox / retention / import jobs, `python -m src.worker`, CPU only, metrics `:9108`), `admin`, `nginx` (:80). Optional: `-f docker-compose.observability.yml` adds `prometheus` (:9090), `grafana` (:3000, needs `GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD`) and `otel-collector`.

### Local InsightFace (DPU holds GPUs)

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.gpu.yml up -d --build
```

`docker-compose.gpu.yml` starts **two API processes** on a dual-GPU host:

| Container | Pin | Workers |
|-----------|-----|---------|
| `dpu-api` | `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0` | `FACE_GPU_WORKERS` (default 2) |
| `dpu-api-gpu1` | `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1` | same |
| `dpu-nginx` | mounts `docker/nginx/default.dual-gpu.conf` | `upstream least_conn` → both APIs |

Each process sees a single device as `cuda:0`. Do **not** set `FACE_DEVICES=cuda:0,cuda:1` inside one process expecting both cards — pin failed historically without `provider_options` + separate processes.

### BFF (Face Core holds the GPUs)

`-f docker-compose.face-core.yml` after `docker network create face-net` (same host). Image is `API-Fast/Dockerfile.bff` (SDK baked in; sibling `../face-core/sdk/python` required at build). `FACE_CORE_API_KEY` has no default. `scripts/deploy-stack.sh` starts face-core first.

**Remote Core:** `-f docker-compose.face-core-remote.yml` with `FACE_CORE_URL=http://<host>:8081` (Face Core must publish LAN — sibling `docker-compose.publish-lan.yml`). Prefer dual-API above for single-host saturation; Face Core when scaling across hosts / many API replicas. Identify ceilings: `docs/FACE-CORE-IDENTIFY-CAPACITY.md` §6.7.

### Loadtest generator

`-f docker-compose.loadtest.yml --profile loadtest` → `loadgen` service hits `http://nginx:80`. See [docs/KIOSK-LOADTEST-SATURATION.md](../../docs/KIOSK-LOADTEST-SATURATION.md).

All services: `restart: unless-stopped`, `json-file` log rotation, healthchecks (`api` → `/ready`, `worker` → `:9108/metrics`, `nginx` → `/health`).

## Required env

- `SECRET_KEY` ≥ 32 chars — `api` exits at import otherwise (`AUTH_FAIL_FAST`)
- Dual-GPU overlay sets `FACE_DEVICES=cuda:0` + `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` per service; override `FACE_GPU_WORKERS` (default 2, ONNX can oversubscribe)
- `EXPOSE_API_DOCS=false` in production; nginx also returns 404 for `/docs`, `/redoc`, `/openapi.json`

## Rebuild matrix

| Change | Rebuild |
|--------|---------|
| `API-Fast/src/**` | `api`, `api-gpu1` **and** `worker` (same image) |
| `Web-Manage/**` | `admin` |
| `docker/nginx/default.conf` or `default.dual-gpu.conf` | `nginx` |
| `docker-compose.face-core.yml`, `API-Fast/Dockerfile.bff` | `api` (needs sibling face-core SDK) |

API volumes persist `enrolled_images` / `uploaded_images` / `temp_images` / `import_jobs` (shared with `worker`) only — **not** source code. Recreate nginx together with the APIs so upstream IPs stay fresh.

## Nginx

- Single-GPU / CPU: `default.conf` uses Docker DNS `127.0.0.11` + variable `proxy_pass` (avoid stale IP 502)
- Dual-GPU: `default.dual-gpu.conf` — `upstream dpu_api { least_conn; server api:8000; server api-gpu1:8000; }` (WS sticky per connection)
- Face WS: `location ^~ /face/ws/` with Upgrade + long timeouts **before** the general `/face` regex
- Uploads: `client_max_body_size 500m` (http + `/employees/.../import`); import `proxy_read_timeout 3600s`
- HTTPS 413: drop `docker/nginx/host-upload-limit.conf` onto the **host** TLS nginx (`/etc/nginx/conf.d/`)
- Proxy prefixes: auth, members, face, timestamp, system, dashboard, images, enrolled_images, notifications, health, ready, metrics
- Security headers (`X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, CSP) are set in `default.conf`; HSTS belongs on the host TLS nginx (`tls-edge.example.conf`)

## Health

- API healthcheck hits `/ready` (DB ping + GPU queue started)
- After recreate: `GET /health` → 200, `GET /ready` → 200, `GET /companys` without token → 401, then `GET /face/queue-stats` with a Bearer token
- Dual-GPU: expect both `dpu-api` and `dpu-api-gpu1` healthy; `nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps` should show a python process on **each** GPU after first inference
- Backups: `scripts/backup.sh` (pg_dump); see `docs/RUNBOOK.md`
